  "critical": false,
  "description": "Braking system that converts the train's kinetic energy back into electrical energy via the traction motors acting as generators, returning it to the catenary (or to an on-board resistor/dissipation grid if the line cannot accept reverse power). Recovers 10-25% of traction energy on stopping-and-starting passenger services. Covers blending regenerative with friction braking, line receptivity, and energy storage fallbacks.",
  "early_win": false,
